            "review_title": "Review at Dlai Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Mackster68\nBrisbane, Australia37 contributions\n0\nThe vibe was weird.\nApr 2019 • Family\nI don't really know where to start. \nWe had 10 people visiting and asked to sit upstairs to escape the smoking group of diners, to which we were told no. Fair enough, except other people were able to eat upstairs? We ordered drinks for our kids, which were hot. Surely a restaurant would have drinks cold and in a refrigerator? We ordered tiger beers only to be told they also weren't cold, however, miraculously the more expensive Heineken beer was cold. \nNow as for the food, well, I could have eaten better by heating up some 3 minute noodles from a shop and munching on a packet of pringles. I am not fussy, nor precious with food but this was really disappointing and not at all nice. When we went to pay the bill, we noticed that we had been charged for being provided with an actual napkin. Very poor form. \nThe young girl attending to us did her best and to be fair, tried hard to offer good service. As for everything else about this really unpleasant, unfriendly so called restaurant, 1 star is being generous. I think I will eat street food instead and take the risk. At least our party of 10 might receive an actual smile and welcome.\nRead more\nWritten April 11, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
